{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"Profiling found a particularly wasteful path: three separate head-layout copies plus concatenation for Q/K/V, and two full-tensor kernels for the softmax derivative. I’m replacing those with single-pass Triton kernels while leaving every GEMM and every numerically sensitive reduction on the exact PyTorch path. I’m also reusing the identical `sqrt(var + eps)` and `x - mean` values instead of recomputing them."}}
