{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"agent_message","text":"The first fused reduction is faster but its generic tree order is visibly different, so it is not admissible. I’m now matching ROCm’s actual reduction structure explicitly: 512 workers each combine indices `i` and `i+512`, reduce within 64-lane wavefronts, then reduce the eight wave sums. This targets bitwise equivalence rather than relying on Triton’s default tree."}}
