{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"agent_message","text":"The discrepancy is isolated: Triton’s `sqrt` differs by one ULP from PyTorch for about 14% of rows, while the centered and multiplication-only intermediates are bitwise exact. I’m keeping PyTorch’s tiny `sqrt(var + eps)` computation and feeding that saved result into the fused kernel; this preserves the reference rounding while retaining most of the launch and memory savings."}}
